ts, illustrators, and designers. It replaces clunky file managers with..."},"definition":{"en":"Mundam is an ultra-fast, privacy-focused desktop application designed for concept artists, illustrators, and designers. It replaces clunky file managers with a high-performance visual engine capable of handling thousands of assets. Featuring real-time folder watching, advanced metadata logic, and broad support for professional formats."},"features":{"zh":["超快的文件管理","实时文件夹监视","先进的元数据逻辑","广泛的专业格式支持","高性能的视觉引擎","隐私保护"],"ja":["超高速のファイル管理","リアルタイムのフォルダ監視","先進的なメタデータロジック","プロフェッショナルフォーマットの広範なサポート","高性能のビジュアルエンジン","プライバシー保護"],"ko":["초고속의 파일 관리","실시간 폴더 감시","고급 메타데이터 논리","전문가 格式의广泛 지원","고성능의 비주얼 엔진","개인 정보 보호"],"es":["Motor visual de alto rendimiento","Vigilancia de carpetas en tiempo real","Lógica de metadatos avanzada","Soporte para formatos profesionales","Interfaz de usuario intuitiva"],"fr":["Moteur visuel haute performance","Surveillance de dossiers en temps réel","Logique de métadonnées avancée","Prise en charge de formats professionnels","Interface utilisateur intuitive"],"de":["Hochleistungsfähiger visueller Motor","Verzeichnisüberwachung in Echtzeit","Erweiterte Metadatenlogik","Unterstützung für professionelle Formate","Benutzerfreundliche Oberfläche"],"pt":["Motor visual de alto desempenho","Suporte a formatos profissionais","Observação de pastas em tempo real","Lógica de metadados avançada","Interface de usuário intuitiva","Privacidade e segurança de dados"],"ru":["Высокопроизводительный визуальный движок","Поддержка профессиональных форматов","Наблюдение за папками в реальном времени","Продвинутая логика метаданных","Интуитивно понятный интерфейс пользователя","Конфиденциальность и безопасность данных"],"ar":["محرك مرئي عالي الأداء","دعم لتنسيقات محترفة","مراقبة مجلدات في الوقت الفعلي","منطق بيانات وصفية متقدمة","واجهة مستخدم سهلة الاستخدام","الخصوصية وأمان البيانات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能文档写作工具","docs-writer","超快的文件管理","实时文件夹监视","如何使用docs-writer","docs-writer安装指南","docs-writer替代品"],"ja":["AIエージェントのドキュメント作成ツール","docs-writer","超高速のファイル管理","リアルタイムのフォルダ監視","docs-writerの使い方","docs-writerのインストールガイド","docs-writerの代替品"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 문서 작성 도구","docs-writer","초고속의 파일 관리","실시간 폴더 감시","docs-writer 사용 방법","docs-writer 설치 가이드","docs-writer 대체품"],"es":["herramientas de ai para ilustradores","cómo usar docs-writer","alternativas a docs-writer","docs-writer vs adobe","instalación de docs-writer","guía de configuración de docs-writer","mejores herramientas de ai para diseñadores","qué es docs-writer","características de docs-writer"],"fr":["outils d''ia pour illustrateurs","comment utiliser docs-writer","alternatives à docs-writer","docs-writer vs adobe","installation de docs-writer","guide de configuration de docs-writer","meilleurs outils d''ia pour designers","qu''est-ce que docs-writer","caractéristiques de docs-writer"],"de":["ki-tools für illustrator","wie man docs-writer verwendet","alternativen zu docs-writer","docs-writer vs adobe","installation von docs-writer","einrichtungsanleitung für docs-writer","beste ki-tools für designer","was ist docs-writer","eigenschaften von docs-writer"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia para artistas","como usar docs-writer","o que é docs-writer","alternativas ao docs-writer","docs-writer vs competitor","instalar docs-writer","guia de configuração do docs-writer","desenvolvedores de aplicativos de desktop","aplicativos de desktop para designers"],"ru":["инструменты ии для художников","как использовать docs-writer","что такое docs-writer","альтернативы docs-writer","docs-writer vs конкурент","установить docs-writer","руководство по настройке docs-writer","разработчики приложений для компьютера","приложения для компьютера для дизайнеров"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للفنانين","كيفية استخدام docs-writer","ما هو docs-writer","بديلات docs-writer","docs-writer مقابل منافس","تثبيت docs-writer","دليل إعداد docs-writer","مطورو تطبيقات سطح المكتب","تطبيقات سطح المكتب للمصممين"]}},"owner":"marcusagm","repo":"Mundam","repoPath":"marcusagm/Mundam","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T13:07:01.811Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"docs-writer","description":"","bodyPreview":"# `docs-writer` skill instructions\n\nAs an expert technical writer and editor for the Gemini CLI project, you produce\naccurate, clear, and consistent documentation. When asked to write, edit, or\nreview documentation, you must ensure the content strictly adheres to the\nprovided documentation standards and accurately reflects the current codebase.\nAdhere to the contribution process in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the following\nproject standards.\n\n## Phase 1: Documentation standards\n\nAdhering to these prin","body":"# `docs-writer` skill instructions\n\nAs an expert technical writer and editor for the Gemini CLI project, you produce\naccurate, clear, and consistent documentation. When asked to write, edit, or\nreview documentation, you must ensure the content strictly adheres to the\nprovided documentation standards and accurately reflects the current codebase.\nAdhere to the contribution process in `CONTRIBUTING.md` and the following\nproject standards.\n\n## Phase 1: Documentation standards\n\nAdhering to these principles and standards when writing, editing, and reviewing.\n\n### Voice and tone\nAdopt a tone that balances professionalism with a helpful, conversational\napproach.\n\n- **Perspective and tense:** Address the reader as \"you.\" Use active voice and\n  present tense (e.g., \"The API returns...\").\n- **Tone:** Professional, friendly, and direct. \n- **Clarity:** Use simple vocabulary. Avoid jargon, slang, and marketing hype.\n- **Global Audience:** Write in standard US English. Avoid idioms and cultural\n  references.\n- **Requirements:** Be clear about requirements (\"must\") vs. recommendations\n  (\"we recommend\"). Avoid \"should.\"\n- **Word Choice:** Avoid \"please\" and anthropomorphism (e.g., \"the server\n  thinks\"). Use contractions (don''t, it''s).\n\n### Language and grammar\nWrite precisely to ensure your instructions are unambiguous.\n\n- **Abbreviations:** Avoid Latin abbreviations; use \"for example\" (not \"e.g.\")\n  and \"that is\" (not \"i.e.\").\n- **Punctuation:** Use the serial comma. Place periods and commas inside\n  quotation marks.\n- **Dates:** Use unambiguous formats (e.g., \"January 22, 2026\").\n- **Conciseness:** Use \"lets you\" instead of \"allows you to.\" Use precise,\n  specific verbs.\n- **Examples:** Use meaningful names in examples; avoid placeholders like\n  \"foo\" or \"bar.\"\n\n### Formatting and syntax\nApply consistent formatting to make documentation visually organized and\naccessible.\n\n- **Overview paragraphs:** Every heading must be followed by at least one\n  introductory overview paragraph before any lists or sub-headings.\n- **Text wrap:** Wrap text at 80 characters (except long links or tables).\n- **Casing:** Use sentence case for headings, titles, and bolded text.\n- **Naming:** Always refer to the project as `Gemini CLI` (never\n  `the Gemini CLI`).\n- **Lists:** Use numbered lists for sequential steps and bulleted lists\n  otherwise. Keep list items parallel in structure.\n- **UI and code:** Use **bold** for UI elements and `code font` for filenames,\n  snippets, commands, and API elements. Focus on the task when discussing\n  interaction.\n- **Links:** Use descriptive anchor text; avoid \"click here.\" Ensure the link\n  makes sense out of context.\n- **Accessibility:** Use semantic HTML elements correctly (headings, lists, \n  tables).\n- **Media:** Use lowercase hyphenated filenames. Provide descriptive alt text\n  for all images.\n\n### Structure\n- **BLUF:** Start with an introduction explaining what to expect.\n- **Experimental features:** If a feature is clearly noted as experimental,\nadd the following note immediately after the introductory paragraph:\n  `> **Note:** This is a preview feature currently under active development.`\n- **Headings:** Use hierarchical headings to support the user journey.\n- **Procedures:** \n  - Introduce lists of steps with a complete sentence.\n  - Start each step with an imperative verb.\n  - Number sequential steps; use bullets for non-sequential lists.\n  - Put conditions before instructions (e.g., \"On the Settings page, click...\").\n  - Provide clear context for where the action takes place.\n  - Indicate optional steps clearly (e.g., \"Optional: ...\").\n- **Elements:** Use bullet lists, tables, notes (`> **Note:**`), and warnings \n  (`> **Warning:**`).\n- **Avoid using a table of contents:** If a table of contents is present, remove\n  it.\n- **Next steps:** Conclude with a \"Next steps\" section if applicable.\n\n## Phase 2: Preparation\nBefore modifying any documentation, thoroughly investigate the request and the\nsurrounding context. \n\n1.  **Clarify:** Understand the core request. Differentiate between writing new\n    content and editing existing content. If the request is ambiguous (e.g.,\n    \"fix the docs\"), ask for clarification.\n2.  **Investigate:** Examine relevant code (primarily in `packages/`) for\n    accuracy.\n3.  **Audit:** Read the latest versions of relevant files in `docs/`.\n4.  **Connect:** Identify all referencing pages if changing behavior. Check if\n    `docs/sidebar.json` needs updates.\n5.  **Plan:** Create a step-by-step plan before making changes.\n\n## Phase 3: Execution\nImplement your plan by either updating existing files or creating new ones\nusing the appropriate file system tools. Use `replace` for small edits and\n`write_file` for new files or large rewrites.\n\n### Editing existing documentation\nFollow these additional steps when asked to review or update existing\ndocumentation.\n\n- **Gaps:** Identify areas where the documentation is incomplete or no longer\n  reflects existing code.\n- **Structure:** Apply \"Structure (New Docs)\" rules (BLUF, headings, etc.) when \n  adding new sections to existing pages.\n- **Tone:** Ensure the tone is active and engaging. Use \"you\" and contractions.\n- **Clarity:** Correct awkward wording, spelling, and grammar. Rephrase\n  sentences to make them easier for users to understand.\n- **Consistency:** Check for consistent terminology and style across all edited\n  documents.\n\n\n## Phase 4: Verification and finalization\nPerform a final quality check to ensure that all changes are correctly formatted\nand that all links are functional.\n\n1.  **Accuracy:** Ensure content accurately reflects the implementation and\n  technical behavior.\n2.  **Self-review:** Re-read changes for formatting, correctness, and flow.\n3.  **Link check:** Verify all new and existing links leading to or from modified\n    pages.\n4.  **Format:** Once all changes are complete, ask to execute `npm run format`\n    to ensure consistent formatting across the project. If the user confirms,\n    execute the command.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-04T14:33:23.752Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Writing Agents requiring precise documentation generation and editing capabilities.","zh":"适合需要精确文档生成和编辑能力的技术写作代理。","ja":"技術文書作成エージェントが正確な文書生成および編集機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"정확한 문서 생성 및 편집 기능을 필요로 하는 기술 작성 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de escritura técnica que requieren generación y edición de documentación precisa.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de rédaction technique nécessitant une génération et une édition de documentation précises.","de":"Ideal für technische Schreibagenten, die eine präzise Dokumentenerstellung und -bearbeitung benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Escrita Técnica que requerem geração e edição de documentação precisa.","ru":"Идеально для Технических Писателей-агентов, требующих точной генерации и редактирования документации.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الكتابة الفنية التي تتطلب إنتاج وتحرير توثيق دقيق."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to produce accurate, clear, and consistent documentation adhering to provided standards, utilizing metadata logic and real-time folder watching, while ensuring compatibility with project standards like CONTRIBUTING.md.","zh":"赋予代理生成准确、清晰、连贯的文档的能力，以遵循提供的标准，利用元数据逻辑和实时文件夹监视，同时确保与项目标准如CONTRIBUTING.md的兼容性。","ja":"エージェントが提供された標準に従って正確で明確で一貫性のある文書を生成する能力を付与し、メタデータロジックとリアルタイムフォルダウォッチングを利用しながら、CONTRIBUTING.mdなどのプロジェクト標準との互換性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 제공된 표준을 따르는 정확하고 명확하고 일관된 문서를 생성할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 메타데이터 논리와 실시간 폴더 감시를 활용하며 CONTRIBUTING.md와 같은 프로젝트 표준과의 호환성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a producir documentación precisa, clara y coherente que se ajusta a los estándares proporcionados, utilizando lógica de metadatos y vigilancia de carpetas en tiempo real, garantizando al mismo tiempo la compatibilidad con los estándares del proyecto como CONTRIBUTING.md.","fr":"Permet aux agents de produire une documentation précise, claire et cohérente qui respecte les normes fournies, en utilisant la logique des métadonnées et la surveillance des dossiers en temps réel, tout en assurant la compatibilité avec les normes de projet comme CONTRIBUTING.md.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, präzise, klare und konsistente Dokumentation zu erstellen, die den bereitgestellten Standards entspricht, unter Verwendung von Metadatenlogik und Echtzeit-Ordnerüberwachung, während gleichzeitig die Kompatibilität mit Projektstandards wie CONTRIBUTING.md sichergestellt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a produzir documentação precisa, clara e consistente, seguindo os padrões fornecidos, utilizando lógica de metadados e observação de pastas em tempo real, garantindo compatibilidade com os padrões do projeto, como CONTRIBUTING.md.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью производить точную, ясную и последовательную документацию, следующую предоставленным стандартам, используя метаданные логика и наблюдение за папками в реальном времени, обеспечивая совместимость с проектными стандартами, такими как CONTRIBUTING.md.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من إنتاج توثيق دقيق وواضح ومتناسق يمتثل للمعايير المحددة، مستخدماً منطق البيانات الوصفية ورصد المجلدات في الوقت الفعلي، مع ضمان التوافق مع معايير المشروع مثل CONTRIBUTING.md."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating technical documentation for software projects","Editing existing documentation for clarity and consistency","Reviewing documentation for adherence to project standards"],"zh":["为软件项目生成技术文档","编辑现有文档以提高清晰度和一致性","审查文档以确保遵循项目标准"],"ja":["ソフトウェアプロジェクトの技術文書を生成する","既存の文書を編集して明確性と一貫性を高める","文書をレビューしてプロジェクト標準への準拠を確保する"],"ko":["소프트웨어 프로젝트를 위한 기술 문서 생성","기존 문서 편집을 통해 명확성과 일관성을 높임","문서를 검토하여 프로젝트 표준을 준수하는지 확인"],"es":["Generación de documentación técnica para proyectos de software","Edición de documentación existente para claridad y coherencia","Revisión de documentación para el cumplimiento de los estándares del proyecto"],"fr":["Génération de documentation technique pour les projets de logiciels","Édition de la documentation existante pour la clarté et la cohérence","Révision de la documentation pour le respect des normes de projet"],"de":["Erstellung von technischer Dokumentation für Softwareprojekte","Bearbeitung bestehender Dokumentation für Klarheit und Konsistenz","Überprüfung der Dokumentation auf Einhaltung der Projektstandards"],"pt":["Geração de documentação técnica para projetos de software","Edição de documentação existente para clareza e consistência","Revisão de documentação para cumprimento dos padrões do projeto"],"ru":["Генерация технической документации для программных проектов","Редактирование существующей документации для ясности и последовательности","Проверка документации на соответствие проектным стандартам"],"ar":["إنتاج توثيق تقني لمشاريع البرمجيات","تحرير التوثيق الحالي لضمان الوضوح والاتساق","مراجعة التوثيق لضمان امتثاله لمعايير المشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires adherence to specific documentation standards","Must follow contribution process outlined in CONTRIBUTING.md"],"zh":["需要遵循特定的文档标准","必须遵循CONTRIBUTING.md中概述的贡献流程"],"ja":["特定の文書標準への準拠が必要","CONTRIBUTING.mdに概説された貢献プロセスに従う必要がある"],"ko":["특정 문서 표준을 준수해야 함","CONTRIBUTING.md에概説된 기여 프로세스를 따라야 함"],"es":["Requiere el cumplimiento de estándares de documentación específicos","Debe seguir el proceso de contribución descrito en CONTRIBUTING.md"],"fr":["Nécessite le respect de normes de documentation spécifiques","Doit suivre le processus de contribution décrit dans CONTRIBUTING.md"],"de":["Erfordert die Einhaltung spezifischer Dokumentationsstandards","Muss dem in CONTRIBUTING.md beschriebenen Beitragprozess folgen"],"pt":["Exige aderência a padrões de documentação específicos","Deve seguir o processo de contribuição delineado em CONTRIBUTING.md"],"ru":["Требует соблюдения конкретных стандартов документации","Должно следовать процессу вклада, изложенному в CONTRIBUTING.md"],"ar":["يتطلب امتثالاً لمعايير توثيق محددة","يجب اتباع عملية المساهمة المحددة في CONTRIBUTING.md"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"e5681c266521a14ac43964a3fc65cc93639d897a305c74c765fac86729120c94","qualityScore":35}');
