 guía para desarrollar ideas rápidamente con AI","fr":"Le guide de composants pour les Agents IA est un kit pour développer des idées rapidement avec l''IA","de":"Die Komponenten-Anleitung für KI-Agenten ist ein Starter-Kit für die schnelle Entwicklung von Ideen mit KI","pt":"O components-guide é um kit de início opinativo para entregar suas ideias rapidamente com IA","ru":"ИИ Агенты: Components-guide - opinativo стартовый комплект для быстрой доставки ваших идей","ar":"دليل المكونات هو حزمة بدء تشغيل متقدمة لتحقيق أفكارك بسرعة مع الأدوات الذكية","en":"An opinionated starter kit for shipping your ideas fast with AI"},"definition":{"en":"An opinionated starter kit for shipping your ideas fast with AI"},"features":{"zh":["快速开发和部署","支持多种AI框架","提供预建的AI组件","支持自定义开发","集成CLI工具"],"ja":["迅速な開発とデプロイ","複数のAIフレームワークをサポート","事前構築されたAIコンポーネントを提供","カスタム開発をサポート","CLIツールを統合"],"ko":["빠른 개발과 배포","다수의 AI 프레임워크 지원","사전 구축된 AI 컴포넌트 제공","커스텀 개발 지원","CLI 도구 통합"],"es":["Desarrollo rápido de ideas con AI","Kit de inicio para Agentes de IA","Guía de componentes para desarrolladores","Integración con herramientas de desarrollo como React y Node.js","Soporte para CLI y otros entornos de desarrollo","Documentación detallada para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Développement rapide d''idées avec l''IA","Kit de démarrage pour les Agents IA","Guide de composants pour les développeurs","Intégration avec des outils de développement comme React et Node.js","Support pour CLI et d''autres environnements de développement","Documentation détaillée pour les développeurs"],"de":["Schnelle Entwicklung von Ideen mit KI","Starter-Kit für KI-Agenten","Komponenten-Anleitung für Entwickler","Integration mit Entwicklungstools wie React und Node.js","Unterstützung für CLI und andere Entwicklungsumgebungen","Detaillierte Dokumentation für Entwickler"],"pt":["Kit de início para desenvolvedores de IA","Entrega rápida de soluções de IA","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento de IA","Guia de componentes para IA","Desenvolvimento rápido de aplicativos de IA"],"ru":["Стартовый комплект для разработчиков ИИ Агентов","Быстрая доставка решений с ИИ","Инструменты разработки ИИ Агентов","Руководство по компонентам для ИИ","Быстрое разработка приложений ИИ"],"ar":["حزمة بدء تشغيل لمطوري الأدوات الذكية","توصيل سريع للحلول الذكية","أدوات تطوير الأدوات الذكية","دليل المكونات للأدوات الذكية","تطوير سريع لتطبيقات الذكية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能组件","如何使用AI工具","AI工具入门","AI组件开发","AI框架比较","AI开发工具安装","AI项目设置指南"],"ja":["AIエージェント","AIツールの使い方","AIツール入門","AIコンポーネント開発","AIフレームワーク比較","AI開発ツールのインストール","AIプロジェクト設定ガイド"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","AI 툴을 사용하는 방법","AI 툴 입문","AI 컴포넌트 개발","AI 프레임워크 비교","AI 개발 도구 설치","AI 프로젝트 설정 가이드"],"es":["cómo usar Agentes de IA","qué es un Agente de IA","Guía de componentes para desarrolladores","alternativas a Agentes de IA","Agentes de IA vs herramientas de automatización","instalación de Agentes de IA","configuración de Agentes de IA","desarrollo de aplicaciones con AI","herramientas de desarrollo para AI"],"fr":["comment utiliser les Agents IA","qu''est-ce qu''un Agent IA","Guide de composants pour les développeurs","alternatives aux Agents IA","Agents IA vs outils d''automatisation","installation des Agents IA","configuration des Agents IA","développement d''applications avec l''IA","outils de développement pour l''IA"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","Komponenten-Anleitung für Entwickler","Alternativen zu KI-Agenten","KI-Agenten vs Automatisierungstools","Installation von KI-Agenten","Konfiguration von KI-Agenten","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit KI","Entwicklungstools für KI"],"pt":["como usar ferramentas de ia","o que é components-guide","guia de componentes para ia","ferramentas de ia alternative","components-guide vs outros kits de início","instalar components-guide","configurar components-guide"],"ru":["как использовать ИИ Агенты","что такое Components-guide","руководство по компонентам для ИИ Агентов","ИИ Агенты альтернатива","Components-guide vs другие стартовые комплекты","установить Components-guide","настройка Components-guide"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام الأدوات الذكية","ما هو دليل المكونات","دليل المكونات للأدوات الذكية","أدوات ذكية بديلة","دليل المكونات مقابل حزم بدء تشغيل أخرى","تثبيت دليل المكونات","ضبط دليل المكونات"]}},"owner":"robertguss","repo":"web-app-starter-kit","repoPath":"robertguss/web-app-starter-kit","stars":5,"forks":1,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T20:49:59Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"components-guide","description":"Guide to using Convex components for feature encapsulation. Learn about sibling components, creating your own, and when to use components vs monolithic code.","bodyPreview":"# Convex Components Guide\n\nUse components to encapsulate features and build maintainable, reusable backends.\n\n## What Are Convex Components?\n\n**Components are self-contained mini-backends** that bundle:\n- Their own database schema\n- Their own functions (queries, mutations, actions)\n- Their own data (isolated tables)\n- Clear API boundaries\n\n**Think of them as:** npm packages for your backend, or microservices without the deployment complexity.\n\n## Why Use Components?\n\n### Traditional Approach (Mo","body":"# Convex Components Guide\n\nUse components to encapsulate features and build maintainable, reusable backends.\n\n## What Are Convex Components?\n\n**Components are self-contained mini-backends** that bundle:\n- Their own database schema\n- Their own functions (queries, mutations, actions)\n- Their own data (isolated tables)\n- Clear API boundaries\n\n**Think of them as:** npm packages for your backend, or microservices without the deployment complexity.\n\n## Why Use Components?\n\n### Traditional Approach (Monolithic)\n```\nconvex/\n├── users.ts           (500 lines)\n├── files.ts           (600 lines - upload, storage, permissions, rate limiting)\n├── payments.ts        (400 lines - Stripe, webhooks, billing)\n├── notifications.ts   (300 lines)\n└── analytics.ts       (200 lines)\n\nTotal: One big codebase, everything mixed together\n```\n\n### Component Approach (Encapsulated)\n```\nconvex/\n├── components/\n│   ├── storage/      (File uploads - reusable)\n│   ├── billing/      (Payments - reusable)\n│   ├── notifications/ (Alerts - reusable)\n│   └── analytics/    (Tracking - reusable)\n├── convex.config.ts  (Wire components together)\n└── domain/           (Your actual business logic)\n    ├── users.ts      (50 lines - uses components)\n    └── projects.ts   (75 lines - uses components)\n\nTotal: Clean, focused, reusable\n```\n\n## Quick Start\n\n### 1. Install a Component\n\n```bash\n# Official components from npm\nnpm install @convex-dev/ratelimiter\n```\n\n### 2. Configure in convex.config.ts\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineApp } from \"convex/server\";\nimport ratelimiter from \"@convex-dev/ratelimiter/convex.config\";\n\nexport default defineApp({\n  components: {\n    ratelimiter,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### 3. Use in Your Code\n\n```typescript\nimport { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\nexport const createPost = mutation({\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    // Use the component\n    await components.ratelimiter.check(ctx, {\n      key: `user:${ctx.user._id}`,\n      limit: 10,\n      period: 60000, // 10 requests per minute\n    });\n\n    return await ctx.db.insert(\"posts\", args);\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Sibling Components Pattern\n\nMultiple components working together at the same level:\n\n```typescript\n// convex.config.ts\nexport default defineApp({\n  components: {\n    // Sibling components - each handles one concern\n    auth: authComponent,\n    storage: storageComponent,\n    payments: paymentsComponent,\n    emails: emailComponent,\n    analytics: analyticsComponent,\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Example: Complete Feature Using Siblings\n\n```typescript\n// convex/subscriptions.ts\nimport { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\nexport const subscribe = mutation({\n  args: { plan: v.string() },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    // 1. Verify authentication (auth component)\n    const user = await components.auth.getCurrentUser(ctx);\n\n    // 2. Create payment (payments component)\n    const subscription = await components.payments.createSubscription(ctx, {\n      userId: user._id,\n      plan: args.plan,\n      amount: getPlanAmount(args.plan),\n    });\n\n    // 3. Track conversion (analytics component)\n    await components.analytics.track(ctx, {\n      event: \"subscription_created\",\n      userId: user._id,\n      plan: args.plan,\n    });\n\n    // 4. Send confirmation (emails component)\n    await components.emails.send(ctx, {\n      to: user.email,\n      template: \"subscription_welcome\",\n      data: { plan: args.plan },\n    });\n\n    // 5. Store subscription in main app\n    await ctx.db.insert(\"subscriptions\", {\n      userId: user._id,\n      paymentId: subscription.id,\n      plan: args.plan,\n      status: \"active\",\n    });\n\n    return subscription;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n**What this achieves:**\n- ✅ Each component is single-purpose\n- ✅ Components are reusable across features\n- ✅ Easy to swap implementations (change email provider)\n- ✅ Can update components independently\n- ✅ Clear separation of concerns\n\n## Official Components\n\nBrowse [Component Directory](https://www.convex.dev/components):\n\n### Authentication\n- **@convex-dev/better-auth** - Better Auth integration\n\n### Storage\n- **@convex-dev/r2** - Cloudflare R2 file storage\n- **@convex-dev/storage** - File upload/download\n\n### Payments\n- **@convex-dev/polar** - Polar billing & subscriptions\n\n### AI\n- **@convex-dev/agent** - AI agent workflows\n- **@convex-dev/embeddings** - Vector storage & search\n\n### Backend Utilities\n- **@convex-dev/ratelimiter** - Rate limiting\n- **@convex-dev/aggregate** - Data aggregations\n- **@convex-dev/action-cache** - Cache action results\n- **@convex-dev/sharded-counter** - Distributed counters\n- **@convex-dev/migrations** - Schema migrations\n- **@convex-dev/workflow** - Workflow orchestration\n\n## Creating Your Own Component\n\n### When to Create a Component\n\n**Good reasons:**\n- Feature is self-contained\n- You''ll reuse it across projects\n- Want to share with team/community\n- Complex feature with its own data model\n- Third-party integration wrapper\n\n**Not good reasons:**\n- One-off business logic\n- Tightly coupled to main app\n- Simple utility functions\n\n### Structure\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p convex/components/notifications\n```\n\n```typescript\n// convex/components/notifications/convex.config.ts\nimport { defineComponent } from \"convex/server\";\n\nexport default defineComponent(\"notifications\");\n```\n\n```typescript\n// convex/components/notifications/schema.ts\nimport { defineSchema, defineTable } from \"convex/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport default defineSchema({\n  notifications: defineTable({\n    userId: v.id(\"users\"),\n    message: v.string(),\n    read: v.boolean(),\n    createdAt: v.number(),\n  })\n    .index(\"by_user\", [\"userId\"])\n    .index(\"by_user_and_read\", [\"userId\", \"read\"]),\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// convex/components/notifications/send.ts\nimport { mutation } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport const send = mutation({\n  args: {\n    userId: v.id(\"users\"),\n    message: v.string(),\n  },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    await ctx.db.insert(\"notifications\", {\n      userId: args.userId,\n      message: args.message,\n      read: false,\n      createdAt: Date.now(),\n    });\n  },\n});\n\nexport const markRead = mutation({\n  args: { notificationId: v.id(\"notifications\") },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    await ctx.db.patch(args.notificationId, { read: true });\n  },\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// convex/components/notifications/read.ts\nimport { query } from \"./_generated/server\";\nimport { v } from \"convex/values\";\n\nexport const list = query({\n  args: { userId: v.id(\"users\") },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    return await ctx.db\n      .query(\"notifications\")\n      .withIndex(\"by_user\", q => q.eq(\"userId\", args.userId))\n      .order(\"desc\")\n      .collect();\n  },\n});\n\nexport const unreadCount = query({\n  args: { userId: v.id(\"users\") },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const unread = await ctx.db\n      .query(\"notifications\")\n      .withIndex(\"by_user_and_read\", q =>\n        q.eq(\"userId\", args.userId).eq(\"read\", false)\n      )\n      .collect();\n\n    return unread.length;\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Use Your Component\n\n```typescript\n// convex.config.ts\nimport { defineApp } from \"convex/server\";\nimport notifications from \"./components/notifications/convex.config\";\n\nexport default defineApp({\n  components: {\n    notifications, // Your local component\n  },\n});\n```\n\n```typescript\n// convex/tasks.ts - main app code\nimport { components } from \"./_generated/api\";\n\nexport const completeTask = mutation({\n  args: { taskId: v.id(\"tasks\") },\n  handler: async (ctx, args) => {\n    const task = await ctx.db.get(args.taskId);\n\n    await ctx.db.patch(args.taskId, { completed: true });\n\n    // Use your component\n    await components.notifications.send(ctx, {\n      userId: task.userId,\n      message: `Task \"${task.title}\" completed!`,\n    });\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Component Communication Patterns\n\n### ✅ Parent → Component (Good)\n\n```typescript\n// Main app calls component\nawait components.storage.upload(ctx, file);\nawait components.analytics.track(ctx, event);\n```\n\n### ✅ Parent → Multiple Siblings (Good)\n\n```typescript\n// Main app orchestrates multiple components\nawait components.auth.verify(ctx);\nconst file = await components.storage.upload(ctx, data);\nawait components.notifications.send(ctx, message);\n```\n\n### ✅ Component Receives Parent Data (Good)\n\n```typescript\n// Pass IDs from parent''s tables to component\nawait components.audit.log(ctx, {\n  userId: user._id,        // From parent''s users table\n  action: \"delete\",\n  resourceId: task._id,    // From parent''s tasks table\n});\n\n// Component stores these as strings/IDs\n// but doesn''t access parent tables directly\n```\n\n### ❌ Component → Parent Tables (Bad)\n\n```typescript\n// Inside component code - DON''T DO THIS\nconst user = await ctx.db.get(userId); // Error! Can''t access parent tables\n```\n\n### ❌ Sibling → Sibling (Bad)\n\nComponents can''t call each other directly. If you need this, they should be in the main app or refactor the design.\n\n## Real-World Examples\n\n### Multi-Tenant SaaS\n\n```typescript\n// convex.config.ts\nexport default defineApp({\n  components: {\n    auth: \"@convex-dev/better-auth\",\n    organizations: \"./components/organizations\",\n    billing: \"./components/billing\",\n    storage: \"@convex-dev/r2\",\n    analytics: \"./components/analytics\",\n    emails: \"./components/emails\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\nEach component:\n- `auth` - User authentication & sessions\n- `organizations` - Tenant isolation & permissions\n- `billing` - Stripe integration & subscriptions\n- `storage` - File uploads to R2\n- `analytics` - Event tracking & metrics\n- `emails` - Email sending via SendGrid\n\n### E-Commerce Platform\n\n```typescript\nexport default defineApp({\n  components: {\n    cart: \"./components/cart\",\n    inventory: \"./components/inventory\",\n    orders: \"./components/orders\",\n    payments: \"@convex-dev/polar\",\n    shipping: \"./components/shipping\",\n    recommendations: \"./components/recommendations\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### AI Application\n\n```typescript\nexport default defineApp({\n  components: {\n    agent: \"@convex-dev/agent\",\n    embeddings: \"./components/embeddings\",\n    documents: \"./components/documents\",\n    chat: \"./components/chat\",\n    workflow: \"@convex-dev/workflow\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Migration from Monolithic\n\n**Step 1: Identify Features**\n```\nCurrent monolith:\n- File uploads (mixed with main app)\n- Rate limiting (scattered everywhere)\n- Analytics (embedded in functions)\n```\n\n**Step 2: Extract One Feature**\n```bash\n# Create component\nmkdir -p convex/components/storage\n\n# Move storage code to component\n# Update imports in main app\n```\n\n**Step 3: Test Independently**\n```bash\n# Component has its own tests\n# No coupling to main app\n```\n\n**Step 4: Repeat**\nExtract other features incrementally.\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### 1. Single Responsibility\nEach component does ONE thing well:\n- ✅ storage component handles files\n- ✅ auth component handles authentication\n- ❌ Don''t create \"utils\" component with everything\n\n### 2. Clear API Surface\n```typescript\n// Export only what''s needed\nexport { upload, download, delete } from \"./storage\";\n\n// Keep internals private\n// (Don''t export helper functions)\n```\n\n### 3. Minimal Coupling\n```typescript\n// ✅ Good: Pass data as arguments\nawait components.audit.log(ctx, {\n  userId: user._id,\n  action: \"delete\"\n});\n\n// ❌ Bad: Component accesses parent tables\n// (Not even possible, but shows the principle)\n```\n\n### 4. Version Your Components\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"@yourteam/notifications-component\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\"\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Document Your Components\nInclude README with:\n- What the component does\n- How to install\n- How to use\n- API reference\n- Examples\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Component not found\n```bash\n# Make sure component is in convex.config.ts\n# Run: npx convex dev\n```\n\n### Can''t access parent tables\n```\nThis is by design! Components are sandboxed.\nPass data as arguments instead.\n```\n\n### Component conflicts\n```\nEach component has isolated tables.\nComponents can''t see each other''s data.\n```\n\n## Learn More\n\n- [Components Documentation](https://docs.convex.dev/components)\n- [Component Directory](https://www.convex.dev/components)\n- [Using Components](https://docs.convex.dev/components/using)\n- [Authoring Components](https://docs.convex.dev/components/authoring)\n- [Stack: Backend Components](https://stack.convex.dev/backend-components)\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [ ] Browse [Component Directory](https://www.convex.dev/components) for existing solutions\n- [ ] Install components via npm: `npm install @convex-dev/component-name`\n- [ ] Configure in `convex.config.ts`\n- [ ] Use sibling components for feature encapsulation\n- [ ] Create your own components for reusable features\n- [ ] Keep components focused (single responsibility)\n- [ ] Test components in isolation\n- [ ] Document component APIs\n- [ ] Version your components properly\n\n**Remember:** Components are about encapsulation and reusability. When in doubt, prefer components over monolithic code!\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:01:28.605Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Backend Agents needing modular and maintainable backend architecture with Convex Components.","zh":"非常适合需要模块化和可维护的后端架构的后端代理，具有 Convex Components。","ja":"バックエンドエージェントがモジュラーでメンテナンス可能なバックエンドアーキテクチャを必要とする場合に最適です。Convex Components を使用します。","ko":"모듈화되고 유지 보수 가능한 백엔드 아키텍처가 필요한 백엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다. Convex Components를 사용합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Backend que necesitan una arquitectura de backend modular y mantenible con Componentes Convex.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Backend ayant besoin d''une architecture de backend modulaire et maintenable avec des Composants Convex.","de":"Perfekt für Backend-Agents, die eine modulare und wartbare Backend-Architektur mit Convex-Komponenten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Backend que necessitam de arquitetura de backend modular e mantida com Componentes Convex.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов бэкенда, которым необходима модульная и поддерживаемая архитектура бэкенда с компонентами Convex.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الخلفية الذي يحتاج إلى بنية خلفية مُتعدِدة الوظائف وصيانة مع مكونات Convex."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to encapsulate features into self-contained mini-backends with their own database schema, functions, and data, using clear API boundaries and microservices-like architecture without deployment complexity.","zh":"赋予代理将功能封装到自包含的迷你后端中，使用清晰的 API 边界和微服务类的架构，而无需部署复杂性。每个迷你后端都有自己的数据库架构、函数和数据。","ja":"エージェントが機能を自包含のミニバックエンドにカプセル化できるようにします。各ミニバックエンドには独自のデータベーススキーマ、関数、およびデータがあり、明確な API の境界とマイクロサービスのようなアーキテクチャを使用できますが、デプロイの複雑さは必要ありません。","ko":"에이전트가 기능을 자체 포함된 미니 백엔드로 캡슐화할 수 있도록 해줍니다. 각 미니 백엔드는自己的 데이터베이스 스키마, 함수 및 데이터를 가지고 있으며 명확한 API 경계 및 마이크로서비스와 같은 아키텍처를 사용하지만 배포의 복잡성은 필요하지 않습니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a encapsular características en mini-backends autocontenidos con su propia base de datos, funciones y datos, utilizando límites de API claros y una arquitectura similar a microservicios sin complejidad de implementación.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''encapsuler des fonctionnalités dans des mini-backends autocontenus avec leur propre schéma de base de données, fonctions et données, en utilisant des limites d''API claires et une architecture de type microservices sans complexité de déploiement.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, Funktionen in selbstenthaltene Mini-Backends mit eigenem Datenbankschema, Funktionen und Daten zu kapseln, indem sie klare API-Grenzen und eine mikrodienstähnliche Architektur ohne Deploy-Komplexität verwenden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes encapsulem recursos em mini-bancos de dados autossuficientes com seu próprio esquema de banco de dados, funções e dados, usando limites de API claros e arquitetura semelhante a microsserviços sem complexidade de implantação.","ru":"Позволяет агентам инкапсулировать функции в самодостаточные мини-бэкенды со своей собственной базой данных, функциями и данными, используя четкие границы API и архитектуру, похожую на микросервисы, без сложности развертывания.","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من تعبئة الميزات في خلفيات مصغرة متكاملة ذات مخطط قاعدة بيانات ووظائف وبيانات خاصة، باستخدام حدود واجهة برمجة التطبيقات واضحة وهندسة تشبه هندسة الخدمات الدقيقة من دون تعقيدات النشر."},"useCases":{"en":["Building maintainable and reusable backends","Encapsulating features into modular components","Defining clear API boundaries for microservices"],"zh":["构建可维护和可重用的后端","将功能封装到模块化的组件中","为微服务定义明确的 API 边界"],"ja":["メンテナンス可能で再利用可能なバックエンドの構築","機能をモジュール化されたコンポーネントにカプセル化する","マイクロサービスに明確な API の境界を定義する"],"ko":["유지 보수 가능하고 재사용 가능한 백엔드를 구축하기","기능을 모듈화된 구성 요소로 캡슐화하기","마이크로서비스에 대한 명확한 API 경계를 정의하기"],"es":["Construir backends mantenibles y reutilizables","Encapsular características en componentes modulares","Definir límites de API claros para microservicios"],"fr":["Construire des backends maintenables et réutilisables","Encapsuler des fonctionnalités dans des composants modulaires","Définir des limites d''API claires pour les microservices"],"de":["Wartbare und wiederverwendbare Backends erstellen","Funktionen in modulare Komponenten kapseln","Klare API-Grenzen für Mikrodienste definieren"],"pt":["Construir backends mantidos e reutilizáveis","Encapsular recursos em componentes modulares","Definir limites de API claros para microsserviços"],"ru":["Построение поддерживаемых и многократно используемых бэкендов","Инкапсуляция функций в модульные компоненты","Определение четких границ API для микросервисов"],"ar":["بناء خلفيات صيانة ومُعيد استخدامه","تعبئة الميزات في مكونات متعددة الوظائف","تحديد حدود واضحة لواجهة برمجة التطبيقات لميكروسيرفس"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Convex platform","Database schema and functions must be defined within each component"],"zh":["需要 Convex 平台","数据库架构和函数必须在每个组件中定义"],"ja":["Convex プラットフォームが必要","データベーススキーマと関数は各コンポーネント内で定義する必要がある"],"ko":["Convex 플랫폼이 필요","데이터베이스 스키마 및 함수는 각 구성 요소에서 정의해야 함"],"es":["Requiere la plataforma Convex","El esquema de base de datos y las funciones deben definirse dentro de cada componente"],"fr":["Nécessite la plateforme Convex","Le schéma de base de données et les fonctions doivent être définis dans chaque composant"],"de":["Benötigt die Convex-Plattform","Das Datenbankschema und die Funktionen müssen innerhalb jedes Komponenten definiert werden"],"pt":["Requer plataforma Convex","Esquema de banco de dados e funções devem ser definidos dentro de cada componente"],"ru":["Требуется платформа Convex","Схема базы данных и функции должны быть определены внутри каждого компонента"],"ar":["يتطلب منصة Convex","يجب تعريف مخطط قاعدة البيانات والوظائف داخل كل مكون"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"7721be98908a4d17c1455e90f01c357c018e1e1bbbde2bdeb0c6810a8de8971b","qualityScore":34}');
